ned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+t &=3 \\\\ 3s-2t &=19 \\\\ 6s+4t &=-10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 19 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -28\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -28\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -32\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=-32,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186393417 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186393418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393417 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74607" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393417 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393417 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $c=⟨3,8,-7⟩$, and  $u=⟨9,22,-5⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393417 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4018a53f-b299-52cf-a135-1013bf76ce32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186393417 #edb/ref 1074 "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 22 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatri